# .NET 10 & Entity Framework Core Standards

## 1. C# 13 Clean Architecture
- Minimal APIs or clean controllers with Dependency Injection.
- Clean separation between HTTP transport, Domain Services, and Data Access (`BankingDbContext`).

## 2. Entity Framework Core Async
- Always use async LINQ methods:
  - `await _db.Accounts.AsNoTracking().ToListAsync()`
  - `await _db.Cards.FirstOrDefaultAsync(c => c.Id == cardId)`
  - `await _db.SaveChangesAsync()`
- Never execute `.Result`, `.Wait()`, or blocking `.ToList()` on EF Core DbSets.
- Use `AsNoTracking()` on read queries to prevent unnecessary change tracker overhead.

## 3. Financial Data Precision & Auditing
- All financial balances and transactions must use `decimal` with explicit precision `HasPrecision(18, 2)`.
- Mutations (transfers, card locks, PIN resets) must record an entry into `_db.AuditLogs`.

## 4. LLM & Ollama Integration
- Stream completions using `IAsyncEnumerable<StreamEvent>`.
- Use SSE (`text/event-stream`) with `context.Response.Body.FlushAsync()`.
- Validate endpoints and gracefully fall back if local LLM is starting up.
